    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T00:47:49Z",
    "body": "Claim released. STOPPED after the same real gate failure repeated.\n\nThe branch is stacked on #468 because both issues change Script::load. Its older base lacks upstream fix 3152dec37fc427e9c3b9ed26c67beddbce5fa748. The app test docs_troubleshooting::troubleshooting_messages_still_exist_in_the_sources reads site/content/guide/troubleshooting.md, which moved to site/content/guide/reference/troubleshooting.md in #1908. The gate failed on that missing path. An isolated rerun of the same test failed again. I did not change this unrelated test.\n\nThe implementation remains uncommitted in /Users/mikekinney/CamcraftPool/.claude/worktrees/issue-2069 on issue/2069-post-sandbox. No push or PR was made. It separates host and user evaluation, applies Boa execution limits and an output cap, and adds the blank template and four preview samples.\n\nAll 10 script_sandbox pins and all 3 post_preview pins pass. The original diagnostic pins failed before the fix. Restoring upstream js.rs and engine.rs made all 8 finite safety/diagnostic pins fail; both endless-loop pins timed out. Restoring the fix made all 13 pins pass. All post suites and their shipped goldens pass. camcraft-post clippy with all targets and -D warnings passes. Geometry, kernel, CL, tools, simulation and motion stages also pass.\n\nThe initial app/UI/workspace-clippy builds were blocked by sccache writing outside sandbox roots. Disabling the cache in the child process resolved that environment problem before the stale test failure appeared. UI and workspace clippy did not complete after the stop threshold.\n\nNo golden files changed for #2069. Two threading goldens are inherited unchanged from #468. #1681 touches post/mod.rs in different functions.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
