    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T01:26:54Z",
    "body": "Claim released. STOPPED under Step 7 after a second real gate failure repeated.\n\nThe resumed quick gate failed operations::threaded_batch_matches_the_serial_loop_bit_for_bit. An isolated rerun failed again. At crates/app/tests/operations.rs:1433, APocket3D refuses tool BN-0600. The pocket is 20 mm deep, but the wider shank starts 15 mm above the tip. This failure is outside the authorized troubleshooting exception. I did not change this unrelated fixture or safety refusal.\n\nThe gate also repeated the known inherited docs_troubleshooting::troubleshooting_messages_still_exist_in_the_sources failure at line 83 because the old troubleshooting page path does not exist. I left docs unchanged. Geometry, kernel, CL, tools, post, simulation, and motion stages passed. I stopped the full gate after the isolated operations failure repeated. UI and workspace clippy were not reached.\n\nAll 13 pins pass before and after mutation. Restoring upstream js.rs and engine.rs makes all eight finite sandbox pins fail. Both endless-loop pins exceed a three-second timeout. Removing the Rust output-length guard alone fails the run-boundary pin. Removing the drain boundary call alone fails the before-drain pin. Restoring the fix makes all pins pass. camcraft-post all-target clippy with -D warnings passes.\n\nThe finished implementation remains uncommitted in .claude/worktrees/issue-2069 on issue/2069-post-sandbox, stacked on #468. No push or PR was made. No issue-owned golden changed. Local evidence is in /tmp/2069-verify and the worktree gate-logs/quick-20261116-010011 directory. A read-only ps diagnostic was blocked by the sandbox; cargo was unaffected.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
